  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">constexpr int compare (<a href=\"#SWS_CORE_02109\">size_type</a> pos1, <a href=\"#SWS_CORE_02109\">size_type</a> n1, <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"cl_ara_core_StringView_cfeb8f.html#SWS_CORE_02112\">StringView</a> s, <a href=\"#SWS_CORE_02109\">size_type</a> pos2, <a href=\"#SWS_CORE_02109\">size_type</a> n2) const noexcept;</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>As per corresponding usage in [string.view] except for the following deviations: 1. The function is noexcept 2. if (pos1 &gt; size() || pos2 &gt; s.size() ) IsoStdOutOfRangeViolation is raised instead of std::out_of_range</p></div>",
